# One URL per line, optionally preceded by `# key: value` metadata lines.
# Copy this file to <your data dir>/urls.txt and run `pa batch` from
# inside that directory. The data dir is whatever your $PWD is when you
# run pa — pa bind-mounts CWD as /data inside the container.
#
# `pa inventory` emits ready-to-paste blocks of this exact shape — the
# usual workflow is to skim the markdown, find a video you want, and copy
# the fenced code block contents (including the metadata comments) here.
#
# Recognized metadata keys (all optional — unknown keys are ignored):
#   title    — used as %(title)s for the filename and embedded mp4 title
#   uploader — folder name and embedded mp4 artist
#   date     — YYYY-MM-DD; becomes %(upload_date)s
#   post     — canonical Patreon post URL; embedded as the mp4 comment
#              instead of the JWT iframe URL yt-dlp would otherwise use
#
# Example block (replace with a real Cloudstream URL from a Patreon post):
#
# # title: Sample post title
# # uploader: Example Creator
# # date: 2026-04-23
# # post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/sample-123456
# https://stream.example.com/20260423_sample_<token>/
